3. IMPLEMENT COMPLETE CRUD OPERATIONS
========================================================

Implement or repair the application's database operations:

CREATE:
When a new student registers, persist the complete account record
and its required related records in SQLite.

READ:
When a student logs in or opens the portal, retrieve the relevant
account information and progress from SQLite.

UPDATE:
When a student changes their profile, completes a lesson, submits
homework, takes a test, earns EXP, or receives mentor feedback,
persist the changes in SQLite.

DELETE:
When an authorized administrator deletes an account or a user
requests an allowed deletion, apply the existing deletion policy
consistently to related records.

Use transactions for operations that modify multiple related tables.

Use prepared statements or parameterized queries for all database
operations.

Enforce appropriate foreign keys, uniqueness constraints, and
validation rules.

Do not create duplicate accounts or duplicate lesson progress records
when a request is repeated.

Protect against race conditions and simultaneous database writes.

Do not allow students to read or modify another student's private data.

Enforce role-based permissions on the backend, not only in the UI.

IMPORTANT:
Never implement account deletion as an uncontrolled cascading delete
that accidentally removes unrelated students' information.

Before destructive operations, enforce the application's existing
authorization rules and confirmation process.

