7. AUTOMATIC DATABASE BACKUP
========================================================

Implement a reliable backup mechanism for the SQLite database.

The backup must include ALL persistent records and embedded file
attachments.

Do not back up only selected tables.

Requirements:

- Create a backup before risky database migrations.
- Support administrator-triggered manual backups.
- Support scheduled backups where the deployment environment
  provides a reliable scheduler.
- Use SQLite's online backup API or another SQLite-aware method
  when the application is actively running.
- Do not rely on copying a live SQLite file alone if WAL mode
  or active writes could make the backup inconsistent.
- Ensure WAL data is correctly included in the backup.
- Generate a timestamped backup filename.
- Validate that the resulting backup is a readable SQLite database.
- Record backup creation time, size, status, and verification result.
- Handle insufficient disk space and backup failures.
- Never report success if the backup failed.

Example filename:

portal-backup-2026-10-22T133000Z.db

Adapt the naming convention to the application's existing standards.

BACKUP RETENTION:

Implement configurable retention, for example:

- Recent daily backups.
- Recent weekly backups.
- Selected monthly backups.

Never automatically delete the only valid backup.

Do not delete backups until a newer backup has been created and
verified successfully.

Do not let a cleanup task delete the live database.

